Problem Description: https://www.scaler.com/academy/mentee-dashboard/class/308097/assignment/problems/29028/?navref=cl_pb_nv_tb

Given an integer A, you need to find the count of it's factors. Factor of a number is the number which divides it perfectly leaving no remainder.

Example: 1, 2, 3, 6 are factors of 6

Problem Constraints
1 <= A <= 109
Input Format
First and only argument is an integer A.
Output Format
Return the count of factors of A.
Example Input
Input 1:
5
Input 2:
10
Example Output
Output 1:
2
Output 2:
4
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Solution :
----------------
public class Solution {
    public int solve(int A) {
        //initialize count=0
        int count=0;
        //iterate from 1 until root A
        for(int i=1;i*i<=A;i++){
            //if i completely divide A?
            if(A%i==0){
                //if I and N/i are equal, mark count as "1"
                if(i==A/i){
                    count++;
                }
                // else it has 2 factors we can mark count as "2"
                else{
                    count+=2;
                }
            }
        }
        //function expects an integer, so we can return count
        return count;
    }
}
